# Project Vortex

> **User-Driven Error Correction Framework & Dynamic Engagement Architecture for Large Language Models (LLMs)**

[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-yellow.svg)](https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT)
[![Python Version](https://img.shields.io/badge/Python-3.8%2B-blue)](https://www.python.org/)

## Overview
Project Vortex is a Python-based prototype designed to solve critical behavioral friction points in modern LLM interaction architectures:
1. **Context Drift Persistence:** Clinging to outdated context roots after the user shifts the topic.
2. **Interaction Fatigue:** Monotonous, overly agreeable, and non-challenging responses.
3. **Forced Engagement:** Intrusive insertion of facts or arguments inside the response body without user consent.

## Key Features & Architecture

### 1. Module A: Topic Boundary Detection & Context Reset
Evaluates semantic root overlap across conversation turns. If a new topic is detected with low keyword overlap, the system automatically triggers a **Context Reset** to prevent context pollution while archiving prior context.

### 2. Module B: Dual-Mode Dialogue (0° / 180° Mirror Engine)
- **0° Precision Mode:** Direct, concise, and neutral delivery for factual and scientific queries.
- **180° Contest Mode:** Adopts a logically sound, constructive counter-perspective for philosophical or creative prompts to foster cognitive engagement.

### 3. Module C: Permission-Based Engagement Chips (UX Layer)
Shifts proactive engagement (e.g., debate invitations, extra facts) out of the primary response body and into discrete user-controlled interaction chips.

## Quick Start & Execution

Clone the repository and run the engine prototype locally:

```bash
git clone [https://github.com/YOUR-USERNAME/project-vortex.git](https://github.com/YOUR-USERNAME/project-vortex.git)
cd project-vortex
python project_vortex.py
